# NET-REMOTE pass 10: A walks a fixed shuttle in B's view (probe --waypoints, steered from the server position).
# pass 8: GpuScene latches PrevLocalToWorld once per frame; the remote pawn's shadow at its feet.
# pass 5: the server's pawn prefab is read off the frame (unread shell + AsyncAssetLoader request), its
# dependency closure is requested when that read lands, and pawn spawns wait for both; the remote pawn casts its
# skinned shadow (70ef84a29). Runner: <scratch>/NET-REMOTE/run_net5b.sh (Editor B joins first; bot A connects
# once B has landed and walks back and forth in front of B's pawn camera, which faces -Z at the segment's middle).
Дано DesertServer --role all on WP_Protocol (--lag-ms 75 --jitter-ms 30 --loss 2) + probe A (DesertNetProbe --bot, player 2, --waypoints "-200,-440,150;200,-440,150" --dir 0.02,0,0: a 400 cm shuttle 5 m in front of B, started after B lands; |dir| 0.02 moves A ~4-5 cm per headless frame = a 60 fps walk's per-frame move) from task/NET-REMOTE
Когда Editor B (player 1, --play --shot-player-view, --net-lag-ms 75 --net-loss 2) joins; B's pawn camera (facing -Z from x=0) looks at the shuttle's middle while A walks it
Тогда net5_remote_shadow B's frame shows A as a solid grey mannequin while walking (no ghost/trail, seq mid-walk frames) with its shadow at its feet; standing A (run_still.sh) has its shadow at its feet and no stray shadow elsewhere; no sync-load for the pawn, interpolation delay 100-200 ms, 0 snaps
# PASS 11-25 (run_net5b.sh, logs/net5b): seq 30/50/70/80 A is one solid grey mannequin (head, body, arms) moving ~5 cm/frame, no ghost/trail; network delay 123-170 ms, 0 snaps, no in-frame load of the pawn; standing A shadow at its feet, no stray shadow (pass 9 still run). The p6-p9 "white ghost with trail" is MOTION BLUR, not TAA: at |dir| 0.5 A moves ~95 cm per headless frame (net clock = wall, ~0.63 s/frame) while DeltaSeconds is the fixed 1/60 s, so MotionBlurTargetFPS 30 scales the blur by 1.0 and it hits MotionBlurMax 5 % (logs/net5b_fast seq 46-52).
